    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d413">

                <pb facs="0526" n="410" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg410"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 702.6211/221.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            German Ambassador</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-04-29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 29, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of the 21st instant in which you state that if the case
                    against Consul Müller at Seattle could be discontinued you would be quite ready
                    to take into consideration his transfer to some other post in the United
                    States.</p>
                <p>In reply I have the honor to say that the Department has by telegraph
                    communicated with the Governor of the State of Washington with a view to
                    bringing about the dismissal of the proceedings against Consul Müller, such
                    action having been based on the understanding that steps will be promptly taken
                    by your Government to transfer Mr. Müller to a post in some other State.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. J. Bryan</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
